  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe `_createCampaign()` function in `DistributionCreator.sol` lacks validation for the `startTimestamp` parameter, allowing campaigns to be created with timestamps in the distant past. This results in permanent fund loss as tokens are transferred to the distributor for campaigns that can never be legitimately processed.\n\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe `_createCampaign()` function validates several campaign parameters but completely omits validation for `startTimestamp`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _createCampaign(CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) internal returns (bytes32) {\n    uint256 rewardTokenMinAmount = rewardTokenMinAmounts[newCampaign.rewardToken];\n    // if the campaign doesn't last at least one hour\n    if (newCampaign.duration < HOUR) revert Errors.CampaignDurationBelowHour();\n    // if the reward token is not whitelisted as an incentive token\n    if (rewardTokenMinAmount == 0) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTokenNotWhitelisted();\n    // if the amount distributed is too small with respect to what is allowed\n    if ((newCampaign.amount * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n\n    // @audit NOT VALIDATED: startTimestamp can be 0, in the distant past, or far future\n    // @audit NOT VALIDATED: startTimestamp + duration > block.timestamp (campaign hasn't ended)\n\n    // Computing fees and pulling tokens\n    uint256 campaignAmountMinusFees = _computeFees(newCampaign.campaignType, newCampaign.amount);\n    if (newCampaign.creator == address(0)) newCampaign.creator = msg.sender;\n    _pullTokens(newCampaign.creator, newCampaign.rewardToken, newCampaign.amount, campaignAmountMinusFees);\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n\n### The Problem\n\nWhen a user creates a campaign with `startTimestamp = 0` and `duration = 3600` (minimum 1 hour):\n\n1. The campaign \"ended\" at Unix timestamp 3600 (January 1, 1970, 01:00:00 UTC)\n2. Funds are immediately transferred to the distributor via `_pullTokens()`\n3. The off-chain Merkl engine cannot process campaigns that ended decades before creation\n4. There is no mechanism to cancel campaigns or recover funds\n\n## Impact\n\nPermanent Fund Loss: Users lose their deposited tokens with no recovery path.\n\nThis violates the core protocol invariant stated in the README:\n> \"Campaign creators retain full control over their pre-deposited funds\"\n\nOnce funds are transferred to the distributor for an invalid campaign:\n- No `cancelCampaign()` function exists\n- `decreaseTokenBalance()` only works for pre-deposited balances, not funds already sent\n- `recoverFees()` is governor-only and for contract balance, not user refunds\n- The campaign cannot be \"fixed\" via `overrideCampaign()` since the end time must be in the future\n\nLikelihood: User mistakes with timestamps are common:\n- Forgetting to set `startTimestamp` (defaults to 0 in memory)\n- Timezone conversion errors\n- Copy-paste mistakes from test configurations\n- Frontend bugs passing incorrect values\n\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n\nAdd timestamp validation to `_createCampaign()`:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _createCampaign(CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) internal returns (bytes32) {\n    uint256 rewardTokenMinAmount = rewardTokenMinAmounts[newCampaign.rewardToken];\n    if (newCampaign.duration < HOUR) revert Errors.CampaignDurationBelowHour();\n    if (rewardTokenMinAmount == 0) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTokenNotWhitelisted();\n    if ((newCampaign.amount * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n\n    // @audit ADD: Ensure campaign end time is in the future\n    if (uint256(newCampaign.startTimestamp) + uint256(newCampaign.duration) <= block.timestamp) {\n        revert Errors.CampaignAlreadyEnded();\n    }\n\n    // Optional: Prevent campaigns starting too far in the past or future\n    if (newCampaign.startTimestamp < block.timestamp - 1 days) {\n        revert Errors.InvalidStartTimestamp();\n    }\n    if (newCampaign.startTimestamp > block.timestamp + 365 days) {\n        revert Errors.InvalidStartTimestamp();\n    }\n\n    // ... rest of function\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add the following test to `test/c4/C4PoC.t.sol`:\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\n\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC is Fixture {\n    uint256 internal constant maxDistribForOOG = 1e4;\n    uint256 internal constant nbrDistrib = 10;\n    uint32 internal initStartTime;\n    uint32 internal initEndTime;\n    uint32 internal startTime;\n    uint32 internal endTime;\n    uint32 internal numEpoch;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        initStartTime = uint32(block.timestamp);\n        numEpoch = 25;\n        initEndTime = startTime + numEpoch * EPOCH_DURATION;\n\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFeeRecipient(dylan);\n\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        angle.mint(address(alice), 1e22);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        vm.warp(1700000000);\n\n        uint256 campaignAmount = 10e18;\n        uint256 aliceBalanceBefore = angle.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 distributorBalanceBefore = angle.balanceOf(bob);\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        creator.acceptConditions();\n\n        CampaignParameters memory campaignParams = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: alice,\n            rewardToken: address(angle),\n            amount: campaignAmount,\n            campaignType: 0,\n            startTimestamp: 0,\n            duration: EPOCH_DURATION,\n            campaignData: abi.encode(\n                address(pool),\n                uint32(4000),\n                uint32(4000),\n                uint32(2000),\n                uint32(0),\n                address(0),\n                new address[](0),\n                new address[](0),\n                \"\"\n            )\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        bytes32 newCampaignId = creator.createCampaign(campaignParams);\n\n        CampaignParameters memory storedCampaign = creator.campaign(newCampaignId);\n        assertEq(storedCampaign.startTimestamp, 0);\n\n        uint256 campaignEndTime = uint256(storedCampaign.startTimestamp) + uint256(storedCampaign.duration);\n        uint256 yearsInPast = (block.timestamp - campaignEndTime) / 365 days;\n        assertGt(yearsInPast, 50);\n\n        uint256 aliceBalanceAfter = angle.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 fundsLost = aliceBalanceBefore - aliceBalanceAfter;\n        assertEq(fundsLost, campaignAmount);\n\n        uint256 distributorBalanceAfter = angle.balanceOf(bob);\n        assertGt(distributorBalanceAfter, distributorBalanceBefore);\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nRun with:\n```bash\nforge test --match-test test_submissionValidity -vvv\n```",
